sparseMonodromySolve -- an "out of the box" polynomial system solver
********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        sols = sparseMonodromySolve PS
  * Inputs:
      * PS, an instance of the type *note System: (NAGtypes)System,, whose
        coefficients are complex numbers
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note AugmentEdgeCount: MonodromySolverOptions, => ..., default value
        0,
      * *note AugmentGraphFunction: MonodromySolverOptions, => ..., default
        value null,
      * *note AugmentNodeCount: MonodromySolverOptions, => ..., default value
        0,
      * *note AugmentNumberOfRepeats: MonodromySolverOptions, => ..., default
        value null,
      * *note BatchSize: MonodromySolverOptions, => ..., default value
        infinity,
      * *note EdgesSaturated: MonodromySolverOptions, => ..., default value
        false,
      * *note Equivalencer: MonodromySolverOptions, => ..., default value null,
      * *note FilterCondition: MonodromySolverOptions, => ..., default value
        null,
      * *note GraphInitFunction: MonodromySolverOptions, => ..., default value
        completeGraphInit,
      * new tracking routine
      * *note NumberOfEdges: MonodromySolverOptions, => ..., default value
        null,
      * *note NumberOfNodes: MonodromySolverOptions, => ..., default value
        null,
      * *note NumberOfRepeats: MonodromySolverOptions, => ..., default value
        10,
      * PointArrayTol (missing documentation) => ..., default value .0001, 
      * *note Potential: MonodromySolverOptions, => ..., default value null, 
      * *note Randomizer: MonodromySolverOptions, => ..., default value null, 
      * *note SelectEdgeAndDirection: MonodromySolverOptions, => ..., default
        value selectFirstEdgeAndDirection,
      * *note StoppingCriterion: MonodromySolverOptions, => ..., default value
        null,
      * *note TargetSolutionCount: MonodromySolverOptions, => ..., default
        value null,
      * *note Verbose: MonodromySolverOptions, => ..., default value false, 
  * Outputs:
      * sols, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, containing solutions to sys,
        each represented as a *note Point: (NAGtypes)AbstractPoint,.

Description
===========

Blackbox monodromy solver for a square polynomial system without parameters.
The example below finds all six intersection of a generic cubic F with its
quadratic polar curve P.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : setRandomSeed 2021;                                                     |
| -- setting random seed to 2021                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : R=CC[x,y,z];                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : F=random(3,R);                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : P=sum apply(gens R,g->diff(g,F)*random CC);                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : PS = polySystem {F,P,random(1,R)-1};                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : sols = sparseMonodromySolve PS;                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : length points sols                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = 6                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : for i from 0 to 5 list norm evaluate(PS, sols#i)                        |
|                                                                             |
|o8 = {4.44089e-15, 1.0732e-14, 1.11022e-16, 6.66134e-16, 2.78677e-13,        |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     2.98937e-16}                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o8 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

For systems with dense support such as the above, the total number of paths
tracked is generally not optimal, though timings may be comparable.



